.Dd 2026-05-31
.Dt NOMAD-BACKEND 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-backend
.Nd show or switch the AI inference backend
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad backend
.Op Cm show | ollama | omlx
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
inspects or changes the AI inference backend used by the NOMAD stack.
.Pp
NOMAD supports two backends:
.Cm ollama
runs Ollama natively and works on all supported Macs, and
.Cm omlx
runs Apple's MLX-based inference stack, which delivers higher throughput
on Apple Silicon (M-series) running macOS 15 or later.
The active backend is stored as
.Ev NOMAD_AI_BACKEND
in the secrets file and is read at startup.
.Pp
Switching backends tears down every active AI LaunchAgent and kills any
orphan inference processes before bringing up the target stack.
Admin continues to reach inference at
.Li 127.0.0.1:11434
regardless of which backend is active; on-disk models are preserved.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm show
Print the currently active backend.
This is the default when no argument is given.
.It Cm ollama
Switch to the Ollama backend.
Works on any supported Mac (Intel or Apple Silicon, macOS 14+).
.It Cm omlx
Switch to the oMLX (Apple MLX) backend.
Requires Apple Silicon and macOS 15 or later; the command aborts with
an error if the host does not meet these requirements.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad backend
Print the active backend (e.g.\&
.Sq omlx
or
.Sq ollama ) .
.It Ic nomad backend omlx
Switch to the oMLX backend on an eligible Apple Silicon Mac.
.It Ic nomad backend ollama
Switch back to the Ollama backend.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-install 1 ,
.Xr nomad-check 1
